# ==============================================================================
# Docker Compose Environment Configuration
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. DATABASE CONTAINER (PostgreSQL)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chosen Image: postgres:16-alpine
# Why this image was chosen:
#   - Footprint: Alpine Linux reduces the base image download to ~45 MB (compared
#     to ~150+ MB for standard Debian-based images).
#   - Security: Drastically fewer installed system packages and binaries reduces
#     the attack surface and vulnerabilities (CVEs).
#   - Stability & Features: Provides the official, production-ready PostgreSQL 16
#     engine with native utilities like 'pg_isready' for reliable health checking.
#   - Performance: Minimal resource overhead with full ACID compliance for boards
#     and tasks relational storage.
POSTGRES_IMAGE=postgres:16-alpine

# Database credentials & host port
POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_DB=task_manager
POSTGRES_PORT=5433

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. BACKEND CONTAINER (FastAPI Python)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Chosen Base Image: python:3.11-slim
# Chosen Tag: task-manager-backend:latest
# Why this image was chosen:
#   - Binary Wheel Compatibility: Unlike Alpine, 'python:3.11-slim' is based on Debian
#     Bookworm (glibc). This ensures pre-compiled binary wheels for PostgreSQL drivers
#     (psycopg2-binary, psycopg) and compiled libraries (uvloop, pydantic-core) install
#     instantly without compilation errors, slow build steps, or musl-libc runtime issues.
#   - Image Size: The 'slim' flavor strips documentation, tests, and manual pages,
#     keeping the base size down to ~50 MB while preserving complete C-extension compatibility.
#   - Modern Python Performance: Python 3.11 delivers substantial interpreter speed improvements
#     (Faster CPython initiative) and full compatibility with FastAPI, SQLAlchemy 2.0, and Alembic.
BACKEND_BASE_IMAGE=python:3.11-slim
BACKEND_IMAGE=task-manager-backend:latest
BACKEND_PORT=8000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. FRONTEND CONTAINER (React + Vite SPA)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Uses a two-stage (multi-stage) build to separate build dependencies from the runtime:
#
# A) Builder Stage: node:20-alpine
# Why this image was chosen:
#   - Active LTS Node.js: Fully compatible with Vite 6, TypeScript 5.7, and Tailwind CSS v4.
#   - Minimal Build Layer: Fast package installations with 'npm ci' and small download footprint.
FRONTEND_BUILDER_IMAGE=node:20-alpine

# B) Runtime Stage: nginx:alpine
# Chosen Tag: task-manager-frontend:latest
# Why this image was chosen:
#   - Production Efficiency: A Node.js runtime is unnecessary and wasteful for serving
#     static HTML/CSS/JS. Nginx on Alpine is ultra-lightweight (~10 MB image) with
#     negligible CPU and memory utilization (< 15 MB RAM).
#   - Zero 'node_modules': Leaves hundreds of megabytes of dev dependencies behind,
#     resulting in a lean, secure production container.
#   - Built-in Reverse Proxy: Directly proxies '/api' and '/docs' requests to the
#     backend container ('http://backend:8000'), preventing CORS friction in the browser.
#   - SPA Routing: Natively supports single-page client routing ('try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html').
FRONTEND_RUNTIME_IMAGE=nginx:alpine
FRONTEND_IMAGE=task-manager-frontend:latest
FRONTEND_PORT=5173
